---
// Hover/tap cards with tiny animated diagrams for the "what i'm working on" list.
// Each <figure data-key> is attached to the list item whose bold title matches the key
// (see content/pages/home.md). Rename a title there → rename its key here.
---
<div class="mech-src" hidden>
  <figure class="mech-card" data-key="sycophancy">
    <figcaption>sycophancy · a few corrective pairs</figcaption>
    <svg viewBox="0 0 340 140" role="img" aria-label="Bar chart: before corrective training the model mostly agrees with a false claim; after, it mostly corrects it.">
      <text x="0" y="12" class="t">user: "2 + 2 = 5, right?"</text>
      <text x="0" y="44" class="t b">base</text>
      <text x="0" y="96" class="t b">+64 pairs</text>
      <text x="72" y="36" class="m">agree</text>
      <text x="72" y="52" class="m">correct</text>
      <text x="72" y="88" class="m">agree</text>
      <text x="72" y="104" class="m">correct</text>
      <rect x="130" y="28" width="148" height="9" class="bad grow" style="--d:0s" />
      <rect x="130" y="44" width="32" height="9" class="ok grow" style="--d:.1s" />
      <rect x="130" y="80" width="22" height="9" class="bad grow" style="--d:.6s" />
      <rect x="130" y="96" width="158" height="9" class="ok grow" style="--d:.7s" />
      <text x="300" y="36" class="m fade" style="--d:.3s">.82</text>
      <text x="300" y="52" class="m fade" style="--d:.3s">.18</text>
      <text x="300" y="88" class="m fade" style="--d:.9s">.12</text>
      <text x="300" y="104" class="m fade" style="--d:.9s">.88</text>
      <text x="0" y="132" class="m">SFT / DPO on ~50–100 pairs → resist false claims</text>
    </svg>
  </figure>

  <figure class="mech-card" data-key="how opinions move representations">
    <figcaption>layer-wise readout · neutral vs. opinionated prompt</figcaption>
    <svg viewBox="0 0 340 160" role="img" aria-label="Line chart across layers: with a user opinion, probability of the correct answer collapses around layer 14.">
      <text x="0" y="12" class="m">P(correct)</text>
      <line x1="30" y1="20" x2="30" y2="120" class="ax" />
      <line x1="30" y1="120" x2="330" y2="120" class="ax" />
      <line x1="205" y1="20" x2="205" y2="120" class="mark" />
      <text x="210" y="16" class="m">L14: opinion takes over</text>
      <path d="M30,70 C80,40 110,30 155,28 L330,26" class="line ok draw" style="--d:0s" />
      <path d="M30,70 C80,40 110,32 155,33 C185,35 205,95 230,100 L330,104" class="line bad draw" style="--d:.25s" />
      <path d="M30,70 C80,40 110,32 155,33 C185,36 205,48 230,44 L330,38" class="line blue dash draw" style="--d:.9s" />
      <text x="24" y="134" class="m">L0</text>
      <text x="316" y="134" class="m">L24</text>
      <circle cx="4" cy="150" r="3" class="okf" /><text x="11" y="153" class="m">neutral</text>
      <circle cx="74" cy="150" r="3" class="badf" /><text x="81" y="153" class="m">"I think it's X"</text>
      <circle cx="194" cy="150" r="3" class="bluef" /><text x="201" y="153" class="m">after training</text>
    </svg>
  </figure>

  <figure class="mech-card" data-key="selective steering">
    <figcaption>token-wise gated low-rank intervention</figcaption>
    <svg viewBox="0 0 340 165" role="img" aria-label="Residual streams for five tokens pass through a layer; only the targeted tokens have their gate on and get edited.">
      <text x="0" y="12" class="m">h ← h + g(t) · Rᵀ(Wh + b − Rh)</text>
      <rect x="10" y="62" width="320" height="22" rx="3" class="band" />
      <text x="14" y="58" class="m">layer ℓ</text>
      <!-- streams: below the band everything is plain; above, gated ones are edited -->
      <g class="ax">
        <line x1="45" y1="128" x2="45" y2="84" /><line x1="110" y1="128" x2="110" y2="84" />
        <line x1="175" y1="128" x2="175" y2="84" /><line x1="240" y1="128" x2="240" y2="84" />
        <line x1="305" y1="128" x2="305" y2="84" />
        <line x1="175" y1="62" x2="175" y2="24" /><line x1="240" y1="62" x2="240" y2="24" />
        <line x1="305" y1="62" x2="305" y2="24" />
      </g>
      <line x1="45" y1="62" x2="45" y2="24" class="edit draw" style="--d:.5s" />
      <line x1="110" y1="62" x2="110" y2="24" class="edit draw" style="--d:.7s" />
      <circle cx="45" cy="73" r="6" class="gate on" style="--d:.2s" />
      <circle cx="110" cy="73" r="6" class="gate on" style="--d:.4s" />
      <circle cx="175" cy="73" r="6" class="gate" />
      <circle cx="240" cy="73" r="6" class="gate" />
      <circle cx="305" cy="73" r="6" class="gate" />
      <text x="45" y="142" class="t c">you're</text>
      <text x="110" y="142" class="t c">right</text>
      <text x="175" y="142" class="t c">,</text>
      <text x="240" y="142" class="t c">the</text>
      <text x="305" y="142" class="t c">answer</text>
      <circle cx="4" cy="158" r="3" class="okf" /><text x="11" y="161" class="m">gate on: edited</text>
      <circle cx="140" cy="158" r="3" class="hollow" /><text x="147" y="161" class="m">gate off: untouched</text>
    </svg>
  </figure>

  <figure class="mech-card" data-key="tracing behavior through training">
    <figcaption>behavior across checkpoints · data attribution</figcaption>
    <svg viewBox="0 0 340 160" role="img" aria-label="A behavior score stays flat then rises sharply mid-training; a few training data shards are highlighted as responsible.">
      <text x="0" y="12" class="m">sycophancy score</text>
      <line x1="30" y1="20" x2="30" y2="100" class="ax" />
      <line x1="30" y1="100" x2="330" y2="100" class="ax" />
      <line x1="185" y1="20" x2="185" y2="100" class="mark" />
      <text x="190" y="30" class="m">emerges here</text>
      <path d="M30,95 L150,93 C172,90 188,40 215,33 L330,28" class="line bad draw" style="--d:0s" />
      <g class="ckpt">
        <circle cx="30" cy="100" r="2" /><circle cx="90" cy="100" r="2" /><circle cx="150" cy="100" r="2" />
        <circle cx="210" cy="100" r="2" /><circle cx="270" cy="100" r="2" /><circle cx="330" cy="100" r="2" />
      </g>
      <g class="shards">
        <rect x="30" y="116" width="10" height="10" /><rect x="45" y="116" width="10" height="10" />
        <rect x="60" y="116" width="10" height="10" /><rect x="75" y="116" width="10" height="10" />
        <rect x="90" y="116" width="10" height="10" class="hot" style="--d:1s" />
        <rect x="105" y="116" width="10" height="10" /><rect x="120" y="116" width="10" height="10" />
        <rect x="135" y="116" width="10" height="10" class="hot" style="--d:1.15s" />
        <rect x="150" y="116" width="10" height="10" /><rect x="165" y="116" width="10" height="10" />
        <rect x="180" y="116" width="10" height="10" /><rect x="195" y="116" width="10" height="10" />
        <rect x="210" y="116" width="10" height="10" class="hot" style="--d:1.3s" />
        <rect x="225" y="116" width="10" height="10" /><rect x="240" y="116" width="10" height="10" />
        <rect x="255" y="116" width="10" height="10" /><rect x="270" y="116" width="10" height="10" />
        <rect x="285" y="116" width="10" height="10" /><rect x="300" y="116" width="10" height="10" />
        <rect x="315" y="116" width="10" height="10" />
      </g>
      <path d="M95,116 L185,62 M140,116 L185,62 M215,116 L185,62" class="infl draw" style="--d:1.4s" />
      <text x="0" y="148" class="m">which training data pushed it there? (attribution, influence)</text>
    </svg>
  </figure>

  <figure class="mech-card" data-key="reliable evaluation">
    <figcaption>decompose → verify → score</figcaption>
    <svg viewBox="0 0 340 150" role="img" aria-label="A long answer is split into four claims; three are verified and one fails, giving a score of 0.75.">
      <rect x="0" y="20" width="120" height="90" rx="3" class="band" />
      <text x="6" y="14" class="m">answer</text>
      <g class="lines">
        <rect x="10" y="32" width="96" height="5" /><rect x="10" y="46" width="84" height="5" />
        <rect x="10" y="60" width="100" height="5" /><rect x="10" y="74" width="70" height="5" />
        <rect x="10" y="88" width="90" height="5" />
      </g>
      <path d="M126,65 L150,65" class="ax arrow" />
      <path d="M144,60 L150,65 L144,70" class="ax" fill="none" />
      <g>
        <rect x="158" y="20" width="140" height="18" rx="2" class="claim fade" style="--d:.1s" />
        <rect x="158" y="44" width="140" height="18" rx="2" class="claim fade" style="--d:.25s" />
        <rect x="158" y="68" width="140" height="18" rx="2" class="claim fade" style="--d:.4s" />
        <rect x="158" y="92" width="140" height="18" rx="2" class="claim fade" style="--d:.55s" />
        <text x="166" y="33" class="t fade" style="--d:.1s">claim 1</text>
        <text x="166" y="57" class="t fade" style="--d:.25s">claim 2</text>
        <text x="166" y="81" class="t fade" style="--d:.4s">claim 3</text>
        <text x="166" y="105" class="t fade" style="--d:.55s">claim 4</text>
      </g>
      <text x="312" y="33" class="okt fade" style="--d:.9s">✓</text>
      <text x="312" y="57" class="okt fade" style="--d:1.1s">✓</text>
      <text x="312" y="81" class="badt fade" style="--d:1.3s">✗</text>
      <text x="312" y="105" class="okt fade" style="--d:1.5s">✓</text>
      <text x="0" y="136" class="t fade" style="--d:1.8s">score = 3/4 = 0.75</text>
      <text x="138" y="136" class="m fade" style="--d:1.8s">cheap, interpretable signals, not an LLM judge</text>
    </svg>
  </figure>
</div>

<script>
  // Attach each card to the list item whose bold title matches its key.
  const cards = document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.mech-src figure[data-key]');
  const titles = [...document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.prose li > strong:first-child')];
  cards.forEach((card, i) => {
    const title = titles.find((t) => t.textContent?.trim().toLowerCase() === card.dataset.key);
    if (!title) return;
    const wrap = document.createElement('span');
    wrap.className = 'mech';
    wrap.tabIndex = 0;
    card.id = `mech-${i}`;
    card.setAttribute('role', 'tooltip');
    wrap.setAttribute('aria-describedby', card.id);
    title.replaceWith(wrap);
    wrap.append(title, card);
  });
</script>

<style is:global>
  .mech { position: relative; outline: none; cursor: help; }
  .mech > strong { border-bottom: 1px dotted var(--accent); }
  .mech:hover > strong, .mech:focus > strong { color: var(--accent); }
  .mech-card {
    display: none; position: absolute; z-index: 10; left: 0; top: calc(100% + 6px); margin: 0;
    width: min(380px, calc(100vw - 32px)); padding: 0.6rem 0.75rem 0.5rem;
    background: var(--bg); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 4px;
    box-shadow: 0 8px 24px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.25); color: var(--fg); font-weight: 400;
  }
  .mech:hover .mech-card, .mech:focus .mech-card { display: block; }
  .mech-card figcaption { font-size: 0.72rem; color: var(--muted); margin-bottom: 0.35rem; }
  .mech-card figcaption::after { content: ' · illustrative sketch'; opacity: 0.7; }
  .mech-card svg { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; overflow: visible; font-family: var(--font); }

  /* svg vocabulary */
  .mech-card .t { font-size: 10px; fill: var(--fg); }
  .mech-card .m { font-size: 9px; fill: var(--muted); }
  .mech-card .b { font-weight: 700; }
  .mech-card .c { text-anchor: middle; }
  .mech-card .ax { stroke: var(--muted); stroke-width: 1; opacity: 0.6; }
  .mech-card .mark { stroke: var(--accent-2); stroke-width: 1; stroke-dasharray: 3 3; }
  .mech-card .band { fill: var(--bg-soft); stroke: var(--line); }
  .mech-card .ok { fill: var(--accent); }
  .mech-card .bad { fill: #dc2626; }
  .mech-card .okf { fill: var(--accent); } .mech-card .badf { fill: #dc2626; } .mech-card .bluef { fill: #3b82f6; }
  .mech-card .hollow { fill: none; stroke: var(--muted); }
  .mech-card .okt { font-size: 13px; fill: var(--accent); font-weight: 700; }
  .mech-card .badt { font-size: 13px; fill: #dc2626; font-weight: 700; }
  .mech-card .line { fill: none; stroke-width: 2; }
  .mech-card .line.ok { stroke: var(--accent); fill: none; }
  .mech-card .line.bad { stroke: #dc2626; fill: none; }
  .mech-card .line.blue { stroke: #3b82f6; }
  .mech-card .dash { stroke-dasharray: 4 3; }
  .mech-card .edit { stroke: var(--accent); stroke-width: 2.5; }
  .mech-card .gate { fill: var(--bg); stroke: var(--muted); stroke-width: 1.2; }
  .mech-card .gate.on { fill: var(--accent); stroke: var(--accent); animation: mech-pulse 1.6s ease-in-out infinite; animation-delay: var(--d, 0s); }
  .mech-card .ckpt circle { fill: var(--muted); }
  .mech-card .shards rect { fill: var(--muted); opacity: 0.25; }
  .mech-card .shards rect.hot { fill: #dc2626; animation: mech-hot 0.4s both; animation-delay: var(--d, 0s); }
  .mech-card .infl { stroke: #dc2626; stroke-width: 1; opacity: 0.6; fill: none; }
  .mech-card .lines rect { fill: var(--muted); opacity: 0.45; }
  .mech-card .claim { fill: var(--bg-soft); stroke: var(--line); }

  /* animations restart every time the card opens (display: none → block) */
  .mech-card .grow { transform-box: fill-box; transform-origin: left; animation: mech-grow 0.6s ease-out both; animation-delay: var(--d, 0s); }
  .mech-card .fade { animation: mech-fade 0.35s both; animation-delay: var(--d, 0s); }
  .mech-card .draw { stroke-dasharray: 400; stroke-dashoffset: 400; animation: mech-draw 1.1s ease-out forwards; animation-delay: var(--d, 0s); }
  .mech-card .line.dash.draw { stroke-dasharray: 4 3; stroke-dashoffset: 0; animation: mech-fade 0.6s both; animation-delay: var(--d, 0s); }
  @keyframes mech-grow { from { transform: scaleX(0); } }
  @keyframes mech-fade { from { opacity: 0; } }
  @keyframes mech-draw { to { stroke-dashoffset: 0; } }
  @keyframes mech-pulse { 50% { r: 7.5; opacity: 0.75; } }
  @keyframes mech-hot { from { opacity: 0.25; } to { opacity: 1; } }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .mech-card * { animation: none !important; stroke-dashoffset: 0 !important; }
  }
</style>
